<title>INDIA: India Crompton 6-mth 1996/97 net down.</title>
<headline>India Crompton 6-mth 1996/97 net down.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1996-10-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six-months to Sept 30, 1996</p>
<p>		    (in million rupees unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net Profit	 160.5  vs    239.4</p>
<p>    Sales	    6,129.3  vs  5,521.9</p>
<p>    Other income	24.4  vs     84.6</p>
<p>    Expenditure    5,476.6  vs  4,985.4</p>
<p>    Interest	   371.1  vs    197.5</p>
<p>    Gross profit     306.0  vs    423.6</p>
<p>    Depreciation	92.0  vs     81.7</p>
<p>    Tax		   53.5  vs    102.5</p>
<p>Note: Electrical equipment maker Crompton Greaves said its other income for September 1995/96 included a profit of 80.6 million rupees on account of sale of investments.</p>
<p>The firm said it alloted 6.61 million equity shares of 10 rupees each underlying Global Depository Receipts in July, thus increasing the paid-up capital of the company to 520 million rupees from 442.6 million.</p>
<p>-- Bombay newsroom (91-22-265 9000)</p>
